WEBVTT

00:00:00.871 --> 00:00:04.270
Cybersecurity professionals regularly make decisions under uncertainty.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:07.520
Threat intelligence analysts evaluate competing explanations.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.120
SOC analysts determine whether alerts represent malicious activity.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.310
Incident responders interpret incomplete evidence, risk teams assess future scenarios,

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:18.300
and managers decide how to prioritize limited resources.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.809
Structured techniques can support all of these activities.

00:00:20.809 --> 00:00:25.600
SATs help teams document assumptions, compare explanations, identify useful indicators,

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.965
and communicate confidence.

00:00:26.965 --> 00:00:29.010
They make reasoning easier to review and improve.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.000
Structured techniques do not replace technical expertise.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.280
They support evidence-based decision-making when technical facts, operational context,

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.090
and uncertainty must be considered together.
